# Open PR branches — do not bulk-update from dev

When something merges to `dev`, **do not** merge or rebase `origin/dev` into
**other open PRs** unless the user explicitly asks for that specific PR.

## Why

Each new commit on a PR head re-triggers **Cursor Bugbot** (and our l10n /
changelog CI). Batch-updating every open PR after every dev merge wastes Bugbot
usage and spams checks on PRs that did not change.

Evidence: PR #90 got three `Merge origin/dev…` commits on 2026-08-13 and a
second Bugbot review; PR #105 got two merge commits and a fresh review after
#111 landed.

## Allowed

- Merge `origin/dev` into **the PR you are actively fixing or merging**, when
  you need to resolve conflicts before **that** PR merges — not as a standing
  chore for all siblings.
- Push **real code changes** on a PR (including Bugbot fix commits) — Bugbot
  should re-run on those.
- Leave sibling PRs alone until their author or staff asks to update them.
  GitHub `allow_update_branch` is off; staff can use **Update branch** in the
  UI when they want it.

## Bugbot settings (staff, not agents)

Cursor Bugbot runs on **every PR update** by default. Optional team toggle:
[Bugbot Automations](https://cursor.com/automations/from-cursor/bugbot) →
**Run only once per PR** (skips later commits — including legitimate fix
commits; use with care). **Incremental Review** reduces cost when re-runs happen.
